apc:IntegerValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte). A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)."@en .
apc:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using apc:pointCount. apc:pointCount takes an integer within the xsd:unsignedLong value space (rdfs:range xsd:unsignedLong)."@en .
apc:pointCount skos:definition "The declared number of points in an unstructured point collection, including zero for an empty collection."@en .
